# A pile of cards
// A game's stock, its discards, a column on the table:  the game names its piles, and says what each kind takes.
// Each pile is its own element around its cards' elements, `<solitaire-column>` around `<solitaire-card>`s.
// A card dragged over it glows when it would take the card, by its own rules (`droppable`).

a "pile" is a droppable viewable list of cards
	its "layout" is one of stacked or vertical
		// How its cards lie:  on top of each other, or down a column -- styles.css
	its "color" is
		// Its last card's:  what the next card goes on
		"none" if it is empty
		the color of its last card otherwise
	its "value" is
		// Its last card's
		0 if it is empty
		the value of its last card otherwise
	its "short name" is
		// Its id, then its cards' short names:  stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓
		set summary to its id + ":"
		for card in the pile
			set summary to summary + " " + the short name of the card
		return summary

	when a card is dropped		-- put the card on the pile, if it is a legal move
		put the card on the pile

	to put a card on a pile, undoable as "Move Card"
		// The card, and every card on it, onto the pile, if the piles' rules let it go and take it
		// - refused, nothing moves, and there's nothing to undo
		// - a game adds its own steps after it:  `after putting a card on a pile`
		cancel if the card's pile cannot give it up
			or the pile cannot take it
		for card in (cards in the card's pile starting with the card)
			move it to the pile

	to test piles
		set the stock to a new pile with id "stock"
		stock's color should be "none"
		stock's value should be 0
		add (a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up) to the stock
		add (a new card whose rank is 7, suit is hearts and direction is down) to the stock
		stock's color should be red
		stock's value should be 7
		stock's short name should be "stock: Q♠↑ 7♥↓"

		// a card is in one pile at a time
		set the discards to a new pile with id "discards"
		get the top card of the stock
		add it to the discards
		its pile is the discards should be yes
		the number of cards in the stock should be 1
		the discards' short name should be "discards: 7♥↓"

a card
	// a card is in one pile at a time:  putting it on another pile takes it off this one
	belongs to one pile
	it "is on top of its pile" if it is the top card of its pile		-- the card the next one goes on
